~ start
Herald: Hi! Nice to meet you, I'm the Royal Herald of the Lands of the Prism! [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/herald_normal.png]
Herald: Oh, this is a disaster! I cannot even prepare a basic announcement with this magical scroll. [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/herald_sad.png]
Herald: The text is far too tiny, and when I use my magical lens to zoom in, everything stretches sideways.
Herald: Look, it is not even a real announcement yet... just placeholder text for testing the decree.
: You activate the Mirror of Resonance to see as she does. [#activate_shader]
: The world becomes blurred, and reading small text becomes almost impossible. [#show_debug]
Herald: Exactly! Now watch what happens when I try to enlarge the text.
: The magical scroll should reshape itself when magnified, but its layout spell is broken.
: Fix the scroll so that enlarged text can wrap instead of forcing horizontal reading. [#minigame_menu] [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/hallway_empty.png]
=> END


~ fail_reaction
Herald: No, it is still broken. [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/herald_sad.png]
Herald: The text still forces me to move sideways instead of adapting to the scroll.
Herald: Try again. The scroll needs to keep a flexible width and allow the text to wrap. [#retry_minigame]
=> END


~ win_reaction
Herald: Ah! Now the text wraps properly. [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/herald_motivated.png]
Herald: I can finally use the scroll without chasing the sentence across the hallway! [#deactivate_shader]
Herald: So, Architect... what did you need me to announce?
: You tell her about Kalipso, the dragon foreseen by the Archivist.
Herald: Kalipso?! Then we must warn the kingdom immediately! [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/herald_shocked.png]
Herald: I will prepare the royal announcement at once!
Herald: Hear ye, hear ye! A great dragon approaches the kingdom! [#close_minigame]
=> END


~ already_helped
Herald: The kingdom is preparing for the dragon, Architect. Thank you for your help! [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/herald_normal.png]
=> END